# Story: As a terminal planner, I want each container to have at most one open booking, so that two trucks are never sent for the same container. If a container already has a booking that is BOOKED, another booking for it (by anyone, for any slot) is refused with DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING. After the first booking is cancelled the container can be booked again.

@draft

Feature: Container Booking Rules

Scenario Outline: Book a container without conflicting bookings
    Given I am a terminal planner
    And there is a gate slot available for the next day, starting at 10:00 with room for 2 trucks
    When I book that slot for a valid container
    Then my booking should be confirmed with a reference and the slot should have 1 place left

    Examples:
        |container|outcome|
        |A-123456789|BOOKED|
        |B-098765432|DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING|

Scenario Outline: Cancel an existing booking
    Given I am a terminal planner
    And there is a gate slot available for the next day, starting at 10:00 with room for 2 trucks
    When I cancel my booking of that slot
    Then my booking should be "CANCELLED" and the slot should have 2 places left

    Examples:
        |container|outcome|
        |A-123456789|CANCELLED|
        |B-098765432|DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING|

